<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cortes of León of 1188</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1188">1188</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> of León of 1188 was an assembly summoned by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ix-of-leon">Alfonso IX of León</a> at the start of his reign, at which elected representatives of the towns sat for the first time alongside nobles and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>. Its decrees guaranteed justice and the protection of property and promised consultation of the assembly on war and peace. In 2013 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> recognised its documents as the oldest record of the European parliamentary system.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cortes-of-leon-of-1188.jpg" alt="Cortes of León of 1188" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Luis Filpo Cabana · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bas%C3%ADlica_de_San_Isidoro_de_Le%C3%B3n._Claustro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
